 "_comment": [
  "LEGACY CONVENTION MIGRATION -- retires the hand-made __mhfastocall / __custumocall / __mh_float",
  "models, which predate the imported Watcom cspec (author: the project's analyst, confirmed",
  "2026-08-03) and declare EVERY register <unaffected> with an empty killedbycall. 23 of the 76",
  "functions on them clobber a register they promise to preserve, which yields NO artifact at all --",
  "callers silently get a stale value.",
  "",
  "SAFE BECAUSE PARAMETER STORAGE DOES NOT MOVE. 47 of the 76 carry per-function custom storage,",
  "which overrides the model (verified empirically: setCallingConvention leaves storage and the",
  "custom flag untouched). The other 29 are __mhfastocall with <=1 parameter, whose sole parameter",
  "is EAX under both the old and the new model. Zero functions needed re-derivation from",
  "disassembly.",
  "",
  "TARGET SELECTION is measured, not assumed: mh_classify_reg_preservation.py decides which",
  "registers each function actually clobbers. Note 68 land on plain __watcall because EDX is NOT in",
  "its <unaffected> list, so an EDX-only clobberer is already correctly modelled there.",
  "",
  "GENERATED. Re-run the classifier and regenerate rather than hand-editing."
 ],
